{{#markdown }}
### Overview

To get fade out effect just set:

```javascript
animateOut: 'fadeOut'
```
> `fadeOut` is the only animation included by Owl Carousel. Add your own CSS animations or use [Animate.css](https://animate.style/) for more effects.


### Important
Animate effects work only with `items:1` and in browsers that support CSS animations and transitions. They apply to programmatic navigation such as dots, arrows, autoplay, and API calls. During drag or swipe, Owl follows the pointer directly and intentionally skips these effects.

### How to use additional animation from `animate.css` library

This demo includes the legacy-compatible Animate.css stylesheet whose class names do not use the newer `animate__` prefix.

1. Include the compatible Animate.css stylesheet in the page header.
2. Set `animateOut` and `animateIn` to class names provided by that stylesheet.
3. When using current Animate.css releases, ensure your integration provides the animation class names and base timing styles expected by Owl.

```javascript
$('.custom1').owlCarousel({
	animateOut: 'slideOutDown',
	animateIn: 'flipInX',
	items:1,
	margin:30,
	stagePadding:30,
	smartSpeed:450
});
```
